<Platform title="Privacy & Data" description="How Digivated uses project submissions, purchase access, browser storage, and site analytics.">
  <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Digivated</p><h1>Privacy &amp; Data</h1><p class="lede">What we collect, why, and where it goes.</p></header>
  <article class="article-body"><h2>Project submissions</h2><p>When you submit a project, we collect your creator name, email, project details, logo, and any social link you add. After we verify your badge, your free launch goes live on its scheduled date. Instant launches go live after payment. Published project details are public, but your email never appears on your listing. Your submission status and any review feedback show only in your account. Supabase handles sign-in.</p><h2>Purchase access and browser storage</h2><p>Gumroad handles payments for Pro, instant publishing and older Prompt Packet purchases. We check your purchase with Gumroad and keep your access in a secure, HttpOnly session cookie. Personal toolkit notes, favorites, and progress are stored in your browser. Use the toolkit’s export controls to keep your own copy.</p><h2>Packet trial feedback</h2><p>The optional packet feedback form collects a display name, the task you tried, your result, and anything you found confusing. Leave out private project information. Feedback is stored for owner review and is private unless you explicitly allow a public quote. Permission is optional and unchecked by default. Consented feedback is published only after review and may appear with the display name you provide. To request removal, contact Digivated through the link below.</p><h2>Emails</h2><p>We email you about your own projects, for example when one goes live, gets reviewed, or places in the weekly top three. If you confirm a weekly digest signup, we store your email and confirmation date to send you new launches. Every digest has an unsubscribe link. Resend delivers these emails.</p><h2>In-app notifications</h2><p>Activity notifications are off by default. If you enable them, you can choose replies, new followers, and project feedback separately. A notification stores its type, a link back to the activity, its time, and read status for up to 90 days or until you clear your history. Feedback contents are not copied into notifications. Turning notifications off stops new alerts. If you also turn on activity emails, Resend delivers alerts for eligible activity you select. You can change both settings in Notifications.</p><h2>Analytics and diagnostics</h2><p>The site uses Google Analytics for visitor analytics and Sentry for technical diagnostics. Project view counts are approximate. Each network counts once per project in a 24-hour window. We exclude automated traffic. The homepage activity counters combine historical recorded page visits with new page visits. The live count estimates how many browsers were active in the past 90 seconds. A daily rotating hash of network address and browser type combines duplicate tabs. Raw network addresses and browser types are not stored for these counters, and no tracking cookie or browser identifier is saved. Repeat page visits count toward the total. External project websites and linked services have their own privacy practices.</p><h2>Bug reports</h2><p>Report a bug opens your email app with your report filled in, or lets you copy it. It includes the page address, screen size and browser so we can reproduce the problem. Nothing is sent until you send the email yourself.</p><h2>Deleting your account</h2><p>You can delete your account yourself under Dashboard, Settings. Deleting removes your sign-in, maker profile and photo, notifications and alert settings, weekly email subscription, Notify me sign-ups, follows and feedback points, and unlinks Google. Your launches are taken off the site. Comments and threads you wrote stay in their conversations, shown as “Deleted account” without your name, photo or profile link. Payment records stay, as tax law requires. Deleting can’t be undone.</p><h2>Questions or corrections</h2><p>For questions about a listed project or information you submitted, contact <a href="https://x.com/digivatedx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digivated on X</a>.</p></article>
</Platform>
